title: '[pallet-revive] Keep issuance balanced when terminating a pre-funded contract'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Fixes https://github.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/issues/12641

    On instantiation the pallet mints and deactivates an existential deposit for the
    contract account only when the account does not already exist, but on termination
    `destroy_contract` unconditionally burned and reactivated an ED. When a contract was
    instantiated at an address that already held an ED (for example a pre-funded `CREATE2`
    address), the reactivate ran without a matching deactivate, permanently skewing
    `active_issuance` (which feeds inflation, staking rewards and OpenGov conviction) and
    burning an ED the pallet never minted.

    `ContractInfo` now carries an `ed_externally_funded` flag that instantiation sets when the
    account already existed, and termination only reclaims the ED when the pallet actually
    minted it. An externally funded ED stays on the account after termination, and a contract
    deployed to the same address later takes it over. The same applies to a minted ED left on an
    account by an earlier termination: it is never paid out to a beneficiary.

    A new multi-block migration (`pallet_revive::migrations::v5`) adds the flag to existing
    contract and delegated account entries, defaulting to pallet-minted. Runtimes must add it to
    their `MultiBlockMigrator` migrations tuple.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: major
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
